{"alias":"/schools/nutrition/programs/farmtoschool","title":"Farm and Sea to School","changed":"2026-09-11T17:09:07+00:00","before":"<p><img alt=\"Farm and Sea banner\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"c0f2c4d4-790e-4977-a83c-04b549b89db6\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Farm%20%26%20Sea.png\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto; display:block;\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Local Foods</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Local Foods Webinar</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/aD5pnaeg_zk\">Local Foods Webinar</a><br />\r\n\tAugust 25, 2025</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"41a4d142-ca53-4090-bf0e-1bc445fa4719\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Local%20Foods%20Webinar%20-%209.2.2025.pdf\">Local Foods Webinar Slides</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Funding &amp; Eligible Foods</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/localfoods/producefund\">Local Foods Fund</a><br />\r\n\tState funding</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"bfbd6609-c577-4257-9827-d463202e9336\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Eligible%20Local%20Foods%20-%2010.9.2024.pdf\">Eligible Local Foods</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"a69c42c6-0342-47a5-aa3a-73e2f74cb6a3\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Eligible%20Processed%20Foods%20-%209.9.2026.xlsx\">Eligible Processed Foods</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Farm to School Programs</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Programs &amp; Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/localfoods\">Farm to School</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/harvest\">Maine Harvest Lunch Week</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/harvestofthemonth\">Harvest of the Month</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/farmtoschool/farmvideos\">Farm Videos</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Maine Fish in Maine Schools</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<p>A partnership with the Maine Coast Fishermen's Association.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a class=\"btn btn-info btn-lg btn-block\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"1413ec8c-1164-431b-8ea1-3d8087016c75\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Maine%20Fish%20in%20Maine%20Schools%20-%209.25.2025.pdf\">Maine Fish in Maine Schools</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Find Local Producers</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<div style=\"position:relative; padding-bottom:75%; height:0; overflow:hidden;\"><iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=1Sj9RmiyCro7PseLaFxx1-qxoX4zptUqn\" style=\"position:absolute; top:0; left:0; width:100%; height:100%; border:0;\" title=\"Map of Maine local food producers\"></iframe></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"dc-note\">\r\n<p>In order to purchase from a local meat processor, the slaughterhouse must either be state or USDA inspected. A list of state and USDA inspected slaughterhouses can be found on the <a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/dacf/qar/inspection_programs/red_meat_poultry_inspection.shtml\">Maine DACF Red Meat and Poultry Inspection page</a>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p><em><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/nondiscrimination\">Non-Discrimination Statement and Civil Rights Information</a></em></p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3><strong>Contact</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Katie Knowles</strong><br />\r\n<em>Farm and Sea to School Coordinator</em><br />\r\n<strong>Phone:</strong> 207-215-6716<br />\r\n<strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:katie.knowles@maine.gov\">katie.knowles@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero\">\n<p class=\"doe-eyebrow\">Programs - Child Nutrition</p>\n<p class=\"doe-contact-link\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<nav class=\"doe-toc\"><h3>On this page</h3><ol><li><a href=\"#local-foods\">Local Foods</a></li><li><a href=\"#farm-to-school-programs\">Farm to School Programs</a></li><li><a href=\"#find-local-producers\">Find Local Producers</a></li></ol></nav>\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"local-foods\">\r\n<h2>Local Foods</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Local Foods Webinar</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/aD5pnaeg_zk\" target=\"_blank\">Local Foods Webinar</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">Video</span><br />\r\n\tAugust 25, 2025</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Local%20Foods%20Webinar%20-%209.2.2025.pdf\">Local Foods Webinar Slides</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Funding &amp; Eligible Foods</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/localfoods/producefund\">Local Foods Fund</a><br />\r\n\tState funding</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Eligible%20Local%20Foods%20-%2010.9.2024.pdf\">Eligible Local Foods</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Eligible%20Processed%20Foods%20-%209.9.2026.xlsx\">Eligible Processed Foods</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">Excel</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"farm-to-school-programs\">\r\n<h2>Farm to School Programs</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Programs &amp; Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/localfoods\">Farm to School</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/harvest\">Maine Harvest Lunch Week</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/schools/nutrition/programs/harvestofthemonth\">Harvest of the Month</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/farmtoschool/farmvideos\">Farm Videos</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-md-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Maine Fish in Maine Schools</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<p>A partnership with the Maine Coast Fishermen's Association.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a class=\"btn btn-info btn-lg btn-block\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Child%20Nutrition%20-%20Maine%20Fish%20in%20Maine%20Schools%20-%209.25.2025.pdf\">Maine Fish in Maine Schools</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"find-local-producers\">\r\n<h2>Find Local Producers</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<div style=\"position:relative; padding-bottom:75%; height:0; overflow:hidden;\"><iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=1Sj9RmiyCro7PseLaFxx1-qxoX4zptUqn\" style=\"position:absolute; top:0; left:0; width:100%; height:100%; border:0;\" title=\"Map of Maine local food producers\"></iframe></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"dc-note\">\r\n<p>In order to purchase from a local meat processor, the slaughterhouse must either be state or USDA inspected. A list of state and USDA inspected slaughterhouses can be found on the <a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/dacf/qar/inspection_programs/red_meat_poultry_inspection.shtml\">Maine DACF Red Meat and Poultry Inspection page</a>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action\"><em><a href=\"/doe/schools/nutrition/nondiscrimination\">Non-Discrimination Statement and Civil Rights Information</a></em></p>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"contact\" class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3>Contact</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Katie Knowles</strong><br />\r\n<em>Farm and Sea to School Coordinator</em><br />\r\n<strong>Phone:</strong> 207-215-6716<br />\r\n<strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:katie.knowles@maine.gov\">Katie.Knowles@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-jump\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":[],"decisions":[{"id":"emailcase","on":true,"label":"Write the email addresses the same way","why":"1 address is shown in whatever case it was typed in. The house form capitalises each name and leaves a middle initial in lower case — katie.knowles@maine.gov → Katie.Knowles@maine.gov. Only the first letter of each part changes, so a name that spells itself LaBreck keeps doing so.","value":"1 address"},{"id":"filechip","on":true,"label":"Tag a document link with the format it opens","why":"2 links on this page open a file — 1 Video, 1 Excel — and say nothing about it, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"2 links"},{"id":"banner-graphic","on":true,"label":"Retire the old banner graphic","why":"It repeats the page title in picture form, which the new banner already does in type.","removes":"Farm & Sea.png"},{"id":"toc","on":true,"label":"Add a contents list (3 sections)","why":"Built from the section headings already on the page. Below three sections a list is not a route."},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Programs - Child Nutrition\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /schools/nutrition/programs."}],"mechanical":["drupal entity attrs stripped: 10","target set by destination: 1","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 4","redundant bold inside a heading removed: 1","images released from inline dimensions: 1","paragraph unwrapped inside a card header: 4","action links marked: 10"],"findings":[{"name":"inline-layout-style-on-text","n":1,"eg":["padding-bottom:"]},{"name":"video-in-a-card-outside-the-top-slot","n":1,"eg":["video inside the card body"]}],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/schools/nutrition/programs/farmtoschool","title